# --- Original game files ---
# Bolo Adventures III (c) 1993 William Soleau / Soleau Software is shareware,
# and its own terms let it be "passed along to your friends or local BBS", so
# the unmodified shareware package lives in original/ (see original/README.md).
# Keep out what the game writes there at run time, and the duplicate archive.
original/BOLO3.SCR
original/_original_archive.zip
# Derived runtime artifacts (decompressed game image etc. -- regenerate from the
# original via the tools; also copyrighted-derived so not redistributed).
work/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  LIFTED OUTPUT — never commit. It is a derivative work of the game.
#
#  Lifting a binary produces a derivative work of that binary, so the
#  generated C carries whatever licence the original does. Committing it
#  publishes the game's code in another form. Every public repo in this
#  family tracks zero lifted files; regenerate it from your own copy.
#
#  Keeping it out also keeps the repo small: stripping it from one
#  project took its history from 20.6 MB to 3.3 MB.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/recomp/gen/
RecompiledFuncs/
